			)
			(property "Description" "Rule 251 (Track Signaled in One Direction): Governs movements on tracks where signals are only configured for  one direction.  Under this rule, signal indications supersede the superiority of trains for movements operating with the current of traffic.  Moving against this traffic direction requires explicit authority (such as a train order or track warrant)."
				(at -3.175 -6.985 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
